    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d93">

                <pb facs="0236" n="144" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v01/pg144"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72119/1404</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Belgium</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Whitlock</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Havre</hi></placeName>,<anchor n="2"
                            xml:id="d93-f1"/>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1918-03-01T12:00:00+00:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 1, 1918, 12 noon</hi></date>. <lb/> [<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Received 5.05 p.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>With reference to Hertling’s speech the Belgian Government declares that its
                    thought has not changed since the response it made to the Pope. It will discuss
                    peace only in concert with its allies. Hymans makes statement to this effect
                    to-day.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Whitlock</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d93-f1" n="2" xml:id="d93-f1-content">
                <p>For papers concerning the American Minister’s withdrawal from Belgium, see <ref
